# Cloudflare Pages redirects and rewrites.
#
# How Pages resolves a request: a rule here is matched first (static rules
# before ones with a splat or :placeholder), then a file in dist (/about is
# served from about.html), then dist/404.html with a 404 status. Because
# 404.html exists, Pages no longer serves index.html for every unknown path,
# so a URL nothing answers is a real 404 instead of a copy of the home page.
#
# Pages that scripts/prerender.mjs writes (the home page, the static routes,
# the topic hubs, every article) need no rule. Do not add a rewrite whose
# pattern covers them: rules win over files, so `/news/* ...` would hide every
# prerendered article behind the app shell.
#
# Rewrites point at /spa (dist/spa.html, the bare app shell), not
# /index.html: Pages ignores `/* /index.html` style rules as a redirect loop,
# and index.html is the prerendered home page now anyway.

